The admissibility check is now concrete: the 163 coordinates are produced from assignments, occupancies, static cross-gain tensors, and six counts/summaries—no outcome or fixed-point evaluation enters their construction. However, the stored 163-vector is coalition-wide; a sealed C1 call cannot consume it as-is because C1 is scored before a coalition exists. The admissible version for this test must therefore rebuild the same encoder for each singleton `(anchor, user, action)`, using only that action plus the reference profile.
