+# C1 resource-context diagnostic specification
+
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. Frozen before any fit for this diagnostic.
+
+## Protocol
+
+- Reuse `scripts/compare_target_parametrisations.py`: exact coalition corpus,
+  split function, seed `20260910`, fixed-ReLU random-feature ridge with raw
+  linear skip, grid `width in {64,128}` by `ridge in {1e-6,1e-4,1e-2}`,
+  validation-RMSE selection, and final train+validation refit.
+- A fitting row is exactly one coalition row from that comparison. A shared
+  per-user scorer is fitted through the sum of its member-level feature
+  differences, so every arm sees exactly the same fitting rows.
+- Exact singleton labels come only from the corpus Fraction receipts. The pilot
+  fallback label is never read as a target.
+- `Q1_ONLY`: selected-minus-reference random-feature design over the sealed
+  16-D Q1 state.
+- `Q1_PLUS_CONTEXT`: the same pairwise design over Q1 plus all admissible 163
+  resource coordinates. Because the stored interaction vector is coalition
+  wide, each resource vector is rebuilt for the singleton transition from the
+  reference profile using the same encoder formulas. The reference resource
+  vector is zero, fixing the exact base-action gauge.
+- `Q1_PLUS_CONTEXT_MINUS_EXTERNALITY`: identical features, fitted to the sum
+  of `own + energy + phi` exact singleton terms. Its reported held-out metrics
+  are nevertheless against the full exact C1 target, matching the stated
+  externality-removal oracle comparison.
+- `LEAKY_ORACLE`: `own, externality, energy, phi` as inputs to the same
+  estimator family and grid, fitted to full exact C1; marked `NOT_DEPLOYABLE`.
+- Each arm chooses once from the frozen grid by validation RMSE against its
+  declared fitting target. No post-test tuning.
+
+## Metrics
+
+- Held-out explained variance `1 - Var(error)/Var(target)` and RMSE against
+  exact full C1.
+- Pairwise ordering is micro-accuracy over every unequal exact pair within a
+  `(world, anchor, user)` candidate pool. The exact zero/base action is included
+  with prediction zero. Predicted ties are incorrect.
+- The same three metrics are reported for each held-out anchor.
+- Leave-one-step-out spread is the minimum and maximum metric obtained by
+  omitting each held-out `(world, anchor_index // 3)` block in turn.
+- Context attribution is one no-refit permutation-importance pass on the held-
+  out set: for each coordinate, permute that coordinate among non-base actions
+  within each candidate pool using deterministic SHA-256 ranks salted by seed
+  and coordinate; importance is baseline ordering minus permuted ordering.
+- End-to-end metric is mean exact selection regret on the parametrisation
+  comparison's held-out pools after adding the same frozen learned interaction
+  prediction to `Q1_ONLY` or `Q1_PLUS_CONTEXT` coalition sums.
+
+## Materiality convention
+
+The context gain is called material only if it is at least `0.0252` absolute
+pairwise-ordering points (10% of the stated `0.650 -> 0.902` gap) and remains
+positive in every leave-one-step-out recomputation. This is a diagnostic
+description, not a sealed acceptance threshold.
